   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.",
   "type": "ResolvingDifferences"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1997-11-12",
   "actionTime": "23:42:44",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 324, the House proceeded with one hour of debate on the motion.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H40150",
   "actionDate": "1997-11-12",
   "actionTime": "23:42:02",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Livingston moved that the House agree to the Senate amendment to the text with an amendment and disagree to the Senate amendment to the title.",
   "type": "ResolvingDifferences"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "1997-11-12",
   "actionTime": "23:39:58",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 324 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "1997-11-12",
   "actionTime": "23:00:30",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 324 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 2607. It shall be in order to consider in the House a single motion that the House concur in the Senate amendment to the text with an amendment printed in the report accompanying this resolution and disagree to the Senate amendment to the title. (consideration: CR H10763)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionDate": "1997-11-09",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "name": "Senate"
   },
   "text": "Message on Senate action sent to the House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionDate": "1997-11-09",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "name": "Senate"
   },
   "text": "Senate insists on its amendment asks for a conference, appoints conferees Stevens; Specter; Domenici; McConnell; Shelby; Gregg; Bennett; Campbell; Faircloth; Hutchison; Cochran; Byrd; Inouye; Hollings; Leahy; Bumpers; Lautenberg; Harkin; Mikulski; Murray; Boxer. (consideration: CR S12271)",
   "type": "ResolvingDifferences"
  },
  {
   "actionDate": "1997-11-09",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "name": "Senate"
   },
   "text": "Passed Senate with an amendment and an amendment to the Title by Unanimous Consent.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "17000",
   "actionDate": "1997-11-09",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 9,
    "name": "Library of Congress"
   },
   "text": "Passed/agreed to in Senate: Passed Senate with an amendment and an amendment to the Title by Unanimous Consent.",
